 "base_ref": "v1.20.0",
 "base_commit": "2e3fe965c963d45ae156c32ef230c7eb7a29a777",
 "issue": 1293,
 "issue_title": "Bug: read_csv and read_csv_chunked use inconsistent skip-row parameter names",
 "issue_body": "### What happened?\n\n<html>\n<body>\n<!--StartFragment--><h3><span>Problem</span></h3><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><code dir=\"ltr\"><span>read_csv()</span></code><span> and </span><code dir=\"ltr\"><span>read_csv_chunked()</span></code><span> currently use different parameter names for the same functionality:</span></p>\nFunction | Parameter\n-- | --\nread_csv() | skiprows\nread_csv_chunked() | skip_rows\n\n<p><span>This creates an API inconsistency and makes it easy for users to accidentally pass the wrong keyword when switching between the two functions.</span></p><!--EndFragment-->\n</body>\n</html>\n\n### Area\n\nCSV parser / read_csv / scan_csv\n\n### Minimal reproduction\n\nReproduction\nimport arnio as ar\n\n# Works\nframe = ar.read_csv(\"data.csv\", skiprows=2)\n\n# Fails\nfor chunk in ar.read_csv_chunked(\"data.csv\", skiprows=2):\n    pass\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nBoth APIs should use the same parameter name for consistency with each other and with pandas.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nCurrent result:\n\nTypeError: unexpected keyword argument 'skiprows'\n\n### Impact\n\nBreaks documented API\n\n### Arnio version\n\n1.1.0\n\n### Install method\n\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.4\n\n### Environment details\n\n```shell\n\n```\n\n### Pre-flight checks\n\n- [x] I searched existing issues and did not find a duplicate.\n- [x] I included a minimal reproduction or explained why one is not possible.\n\n### Additional context\n\nSuggested Fix\n\nAdd skiprows as an alias for skip_rows in read_csv_chunked() (or rename the parameter entirely while preserving backward compatibility).\n\nFiles involved\nio.py\n\nHey @im-anishraj !I would like to work on this!",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1293",
 "pr": 1749,
 "pr_title": "fix(io): add skiprows alias to read_csv_chunked for API consistency",
 "pr_body": "Fixes #1293\r\n\r\n## What\r\nread_csv() uses `skiprows` (matching pandas convention) but read_csv_chunked()\r\nonly accepted `skip_rows`, causing a confusing TypeError when users switched\r\nbetween the two functions.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- `arnio/io.py`: added `skiprows: int | None = None` as a keyword-only alias\r\n  in `read_csv_chunked()`. `skip_rows` is fully preserved for backward compat.\r\n- `tests/test_csv.py`: added `TestReadCsvChunkedSkiprowsAlias` with 8 tests.\r\n\r\n## Conflict resolution\r\n| Inputs | Behaviour |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Only `skiprows` | used as the row-skip count |\r\n| Only `skip_rows` | existing behaviour unchanged |\r\n| Both, same value | no error |\r\n| Both, different values | `ValueError` with clear message |\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\nTwo files only. No C++ changes. `skip_rows` semantics are unchanged \u2014\r\nboth parameters skip data rows *after* the header in chunked mode.\r\n",
 "fix_commit": "53fbf712fb50df2aefef2d8b24c3b0e98dfd51d4",
